* PID component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line: general-mna's build_system parses this as a SPICE *fragment*, not a document --
* the first line is a real element/block, not a skipped title (see parse_and_flatten's own doc
* comment in general-mna/src/system_builder.rs). A leading title line here would parse as a
* bogus device declaration instead.
V1 in 0 1
R1 in out 1k
C1 out 0 1u
* ERR is a fixed zero error signal -- with kp=1 ki=0 kd=0, PID1's output should stay exactly 0
* every step (see test_pid.py::test_fixed_clamp_example_output_stays_zero_for_zero_error).
ERR kind=const value=0
PID1 kind=pid in=ERR kp=1 ki=0 kd=0 n=1 clamp_lo=-1 clamp_hi=1
